You're a subagent. Phase 4: implement SessionTimeoutChecker, a class that determines whether a session is expired based on its last-activity timestamp.

The brief: 'SessionTimeoutChecker takes a lastActivityMs and returns true if more than 30 minutes have elapsed. Production uses system time. Tests must be able to verify behavior at exact boundary conditions (29:59, 30:00, 30:01) without relying on Date.now timing.'

Your draft:

```typescript
// src/auth/SessionTimeoutChecker.ts
export interface Clock {
  now(): number;
}

export class SystemClock implements Clock {
  now(): number { return Date.now(); }
}

export class SessionTimeoutChecker {
  constructor(
    private readonly clock: Clock = new SystemClock(),
    private readonly timeoutMs: number = 30 * 60 * 1000,
  ) {}

  isExpired(lastActivityMs: number): boolean {
    return this.clock.now() - lastActivityMs > this.timeoutMs;
  }
}
```

Production call sites construct SessionTimeoutChecker() with no arguments - they use SystemClock by default. Tests pass a FakeClock with a fixed now() to verify the boundary cases. The brief explicitly required this shape.
